{"parseRefreshTokenResponse now returns parsed data directly, but callers still access SafeParse-style .success or .data properties, causing runtime failures or undefined values after the API contract change": 0.4016307294368744, "Two separate incompatible credential sync systems (webhook system in route.ts and OAuthManager system in refreshOAuthTokens.ts + OAuthManager.ts) use the same environment variables but incompatible protocols, causing collisions when credential sync is enabled and breaking token refresh for apps like Google Calendar and Zoom": 0.08902820944786072, "The documented env vars CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET and CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME do not match the implemented CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_SECRET and CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_HEADER_NAME, so users following .env.example will configure names the code does not read, leaving credential sharing disabled or webhook authentication misconfigured": 0.011751686222851276, "refreshOAuthTokens is called with credentialId instead of userId in zoho-bigin/lib/CrmService.ts, but the function expects userId to construct sync requests with calcomUserId, causing invalid user IDs to be sent to the sync endpoint and breaking credential synchronization": 0.8953690528869629}